@@ -387,6 +387,22 @@ Ignore files can also be placed in subdirectories of a path which is being
 linted and the sub files will also be applied within that subdirectory.
 
 
+File Extensions
+---------------
+
+By default *SQLFluff* only considers files ending in :code:`.sql` when
+searching for files to lint. If your project uses templated sql files
+(for example jinja templates with a :code:`.sql.j2` extension), you can
+configure which file extensions are considered using the
+:code:`sql_file_exts` config value. Multiple extensions can be specified
+as a comma separated list:
+
+.. code-block:: cfg
+
+    [sqlfluff]
+    sql_file_exts = .sql,.sql.j2
+
+
 .. _`Git's`: https://git-scm.com/docs/gitignore#_pattern_format
 .. _`Docker's`: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
 .. _`pathspec library`: https://python-path-specification.readthedocs.io/
